## Institution(ASU)
## MLT(PercentOfANumber)
## MLTleader(1)
## Level(2)
## KEYWORDS('percent', 'mathematics for business', 'algebraic expression')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$a  = random(1,   99);
$aa = random(10,  90,  10);
$b  = random(210, 290, 10);
$bb = random(10,  90,  10);

BEGIN_PGML
Determine the indicated quantity.  
a) [$a]% of [$aa] = [_]{Real($a*$aa/100)}

b) [$b]% of [$bb] = [_]{Real($b*$bb/100)}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Recall that a percent is just a fraction with denomiator of 100. Change the percent to a fraction and multiply. 

a) [`` \frac{[$a]}{100} \cdot [$aa] = [$a*$aa/100] ``]

b) [`` \frac{[$b]}{100} \cdot [$bb] = [$b*$bb/100] ``]
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();        # This should be the last executable line in the problem.